{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"content":"391\n\nTo calculate $17 \\times 23$, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm or break it down using the distributive property.\n\n**Method: Distributive Property**\nWe can split 23 into $20 + 3$:\n$$17 \\times 23 = 17 \\times (20 + 3)$$\n$$= (17 \\times 20) + (17 \\times 3)$$\n\n1.  Calculate $17 \\times 20$:\n    $$17 \\times 2 = 34$$\n    $$34 \\times 10 = 340$$\n\n2.  Calculate $17 \\times 3$:\n    $$10 \\times 3 = 30$$\n    $$7 \\times 3 = 21$$\n    $$30 + 21 = 51$$\n\n3.  Add the results:\n    $$340 + 51 = 391$$\n\n**Final Answer:**\n391","role":"assistant"}}],"created":1788650777,"id":"chatcmpl-1788650777","model":"qwen3.8-27b-q4_k_m","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"cached_tokens":0,"completion_tokens":231,"prompt_tokens":81,"total_tokens":312}}